message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "peclet-coupling: two-way CFD-DEM coupling of peclet.flow and peclet.dem"
abstract: >-
  Two-way coupling of an Eulerian incompressible flow solver (peclet.flow) to a Lagrangian discrete
  element solver (peclet.dem), in the caller's own physical units. Two drivers share one vocabulary:
  CfdDem is the unresolved point-particle driver for dilute-to-dense suspensions and packed beds,
  where a grain is a point carrying a drag closure and the fluid equations are volume-averaged
  (porosity enters the momentum and continuity equations, not merely the drag); ResolvedCfdDem is
  the resolved driver, in which each grain is an analytic signed-distance instance in the flow
  solver's scene, the fluid resolves its surface, and no drag correlation appears anywhere. Both
  codes share one MPI block decomposition, so the coupled run is distributed whenever they are.
  Part of the peclet suite.
type: software
